    "updated_at": "2026-10-28T07:50:33Z",
    "seo": {
      "title": "Sportswear in Iran: Team Kits and Supporter Clothing",
      "description": "Explore a documented Iranian sportswear example through Majid's national football kits, design choices, and supporter merchandise."
    },
    "content": [
      {
        "id": "national-team-example",
        "type": "text",
        "heading": "An Iranian manufacturer on the international stage",
        "content": "Sportswear is one of the most visible connections between Iran's sporting institutions and its manufacturing businesses. A clearly documented example is Majid, the Iranian company that supplied the national football team's clothing in 2022. Contemporary reporting identifies both its use during qualification and the unveiling of a new tournament collection shortly before the World Cup in Qatar. These records establish a particular supplier relationship at a particular time; they do not establish the company's share of Iran's clothing market. [s1]\n\nTasnim reported that the new home and away kits were launched at Tehran's Milad Tower, with the sports minister and the head of the football federation attending. The event illustrates how a playing uniform can become a public presentation involving a manufacturer, a national team, and sporting officials. The report does not disclose contract terms, production quantities, or the financial relationship between the parties. [s2]",
        "source_ids": ["s1", "s2"]
      },
      {
        "id": "design-and-merchandise",
        "type": "text",
        "heading": "A uniform and a supporter product",
        "content": "The 2022 collection also shows why a match uniform and a retail garment should be distinguished. SportsLogos.Net reported that Majid unveiled the shirts through its Instagram account and offered fan versions through its online shop. That establishes a documented supporter product alongside the team's playing clothing, without demonstrating that both versions had identical fabrics, construction, or performance characteristics. [s1]\n\nThe home shirt was predominantly white and the away shirt red. Both used a tonal cheetah-spot pattern on the sleeves. This is a specific example of wildlife imagery entering the visual identity of a national sporting team. The design can be described from the published documentation, but its popularity, commercial success, and meaning to different supporters would require separate evidence. [s1]",
        "source_ids": ["s1"]
      },
      {
        "id": "supplier-history",
        "type": "text",
        "heading": "Reading supplier changes carefully",
        "content": "The same contemporary account places Majid's involvement within a changing supplier history. It records Uhlsport's use around the 2014 World Cup, a brief Givova period, Adidas clothing through the 2018 tournament, and a return to Uhlsport before the move to Majid. This is evidence of changing brands on one prominent team, rather than a history of the whole Iranian sportswear industry. It also does not explain whether each arrangement was a sponsorship, a purchase agreement, or another form of supply. [s1]\n\nThe useful conclusion is therefore specific: an Iranian manufacturer supplied internationally visible team clothing and marketed a related supporter version. A fuller account of the sector needs evidence from everyday participation, women's sportswear, school and club procurement, manufacturing locations, and retail distribution. Those areas remain outside the verified coverage of this draft.",
        "source_ids": ["s1"]
      }
    ],
